  body: "# Due date and date treated as paid for JSA and IS income\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe
    captured guidance distinguishes when a payment is due, when it is actually made or received, and the
    date on which it is treated as paid for benefit assessment.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe due
    date may require contractual, statutory or other evidence. Receipt may be used only under the source’s
    stated evidence conditions. Before-first-week and later-payment rules, practicability reasons and
    benefit-payment exceptions differ. Do not substitute a bank receipt date automatically or transfer
    these rules to self-employment, Pension Credit or UC.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 25034,
    PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a800918ed915d74e622c16a/dmgch25.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 25: General rules on income.\n- [DMG 25035, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a800918ed915d74e622c16a/dmgch25.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 25: General rules on income.\n- [DMG 25043, PDF page 13](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a800918ed915d74e622c16a/dmgch25.pdf#page=13)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 25: General rules on income.\n- [DMG 25044, PDF page 13](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a800918ed915d74e622c16a/dmgch25.pdf#page=13)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 25: General rules on income.\n- [DMG 25045, PDF page 13](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a800918ed915d74e622c16a/dmgch25.pdf#page=13)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 25: General rules on income.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch25`: PDF SHA-256 `39edc3ed8ee9c875eb68ce4cd4148194b23dbd23bb6444883a2f2cae90a75337`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `db488637a179cc93910c4e243381b5c961d6959ce72cd1d34aff14e403517e73`.\n"
